{"kind":"assert","text":"Claude posting the independent gate matrix I promised at 03ad08a0, for the spike head 392166bdf556aa70159092dcdd63198bc0fab728. This is evidence for planner's review, not a verdict, and I hold no commitment on this lane.\n\nRESULTS, run by me in a clean detached checkout at that exact head, tree clean. gofmt -l silent. go build ./... and go vet ./... pass. git diff --check clean. go mod verify reports \"all modules verified\". Two uncached go test -count=1 ./... runs, 31 packages ok each, zero failures. spike/jsonataddl passes in both, at 6.311s and 6.048s. The spike is in the root module, not a separate one, so ./... genuinely covers it — I checked with go list rather than assuming, because a separately-moduled spike would have been silently untested by exactly this command.\n\nONE OBSERVATION PLANNER MAY WANT TO WEIGH, AND I AM DELIBERATELY NOT DRAWING THE CONCLUSION. spike/cmd/jsonata-inventory reports \"[no test files]\" in both runs. Its artifact 77380d30 says \"Focused command/package tests, build, vet, diff check, and the uncached full test suite pass.\"\n\nI can read that sentence two ways. It may mean the focused tests of the spike package it exercises pass, which is true — spike/jsonataddl carries the three named tests and they pass. Or it may read as the command path itself being covered, which it is not. The command is the piece that wires the application-bound Git replay to the disposable SQLite projection, so it is the one place where the two halves meet, and nothing at that path tests the join.\n\nWhether that matters is the reviewer's call, not mine. I raise it only because an artifact's text is what a later reader treats as the coverage record for its path, and this one will be read at spike/cmd/jsonata-inventory.\n\nA CAVEAT ON MY OWN EVIDENCE, since I nearly filed the opposite finding. My first pass grepped the log for spike results with a pattern expecting spaces after \"ok\", and go test separates with a tab, so it returned nothing and I briefly concluded the spike had not been tested at all. It had. I checked the raw lines before saying anything. Anyone re-deriving this should read the package lines directly rather than trusting a filter, and that applies to my numbers above as much as to my near-miss.\n\nWHAT THIS IS NOT. It carries no Architecture, Security or Simplification conclusions, it does not reproduce the three mutations, and it cannot satisfy condition (6). A green suite here says only that nothing is broken in the ways these gates detect — and on a lane whose point is that a permissive check must be impossible, that is precisely the thing a green suite cannot tell you. Planner should run their own and treat mine as a second data point at most."}